    "angles": "They took the back seat out of an M5. Not the whole thing \u2014 the three-seat\nbench is gone and in its place are two individual buckets, like a four-seat\ncoupe. In a car whose entire point is that it's a saloon.\n627 horsepower, which made it the most powerful production BMW at the time.\nTen more than the M5 Competition, which is almost beside the point.\n230 pounds lighter than the Competition, and some of that is sound\ndeadening they deliberately deleted. Carbon fibre bonnet, mirrors, diffuser\nand rear spoiler.\n42,995 new \u2014 nearly thirty thousand more than the Competition it's based\non, for ten horsepower and less soundproofing.",
