  "script": "627 horsepower in a sedan. That's the 2022 M5 CS. BMW produced only 1,132 units of the 2022 M5 CS, with 454 allocated to the United States, accounting for 40% of the total production. Powered by a 4.4L turbocharged V8. It delivers 627 hp and 553 lb-ft. Inside, two carbon bucket seats replace the rear bench. Sporty yet plush. Adaptive suspension costs $3,500 and conquered the N\u00fcrburgring in under 7:30. Originally $142,000, they go for about $172,000 today. The M5 CS rockets from zero to sixty in just 2.8 seconds. It's BMW's most powerful sedan. Do you think 627 horsepower changes its essence?",
